# EXPECT: assigns enclosing name
#
# A `local` declaration that comes AFTER a write to the same name.
#
# THE POINT OF THIS FIXTURE is that "top level" was necessary and NOT sufficient,
# and the exemption written with only that condition let a declaration
# retroactively legalise a write that had already run:
#
#   define b(d) as: x is 1 / local x is 2 / return d
#   VM   6     (the outer x really was clobbered)
#   AOT  105   (the outer x untouched)      both build, both rc 0
#
# The previous compiler REFUSED this program loudly. The exemption meant to stop
# a false refusal reintroduced the silent wrong answer the guard exists for —
# through the guard's own escape hatch.
#
# The rule is DOMINANCE, not position: a declaration only makes the name the
# define's own if it precedes every use of that name in the body. Its sibling
# nested_conditional_local.eigs is the same principle one level out — a
# declaration inside an `if` dominates nothing.

define f(y) as:
    local x is 100
    define b(d) as:
        x is 1
        local x is 2
        return d
    local r is b of 5
    return x + r

print of (f of 0)
